    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="6.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:WlArt">Wl art</ref> 6.1</head>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="la" source="#robertson" n="6.1" corresp="#wit-h">Si autem Anglus infirmus fuerit, inveniat alium qui pro eo faciat.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-h">If, however, the Englishman is infirm, he shall find a substitute to act for him.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="487"><ref target="clause:WiLad_2-1">Wl lad 2.1</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">ebd. 2, 1</note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:WiLad_2-1">Wl lad 2.1</ref></note>
        <note type="editorial">Added October 2026 from Robertson pp. 240–241 (text and translation); Liebermann’s text (K–M) not yet added</note>
      </div>
